<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>
  <!-- GENERATED by design/Jawa/mods/biome_flora.py - do not hand-edit.

       Ash'karr's flora, ASSIGNED rather than inherited. Owner's brief 2026-08-23:
       distribute the plants per biome, avoid using the same plant across different
       biome types, and player-grown flora (tinctoria, healroot) may decorate.

       🔴 wildPlants is a LoadDataFromXmlCustom field: the node NAME is the plant
       defName and its VALUE is the commonality. An <li> here discards the whole
       BiomeDef, silently. -->

  <!-- ============ biomes this file deliberately does NOT patch ============

       BIOMEFLORA_PATCH_WIPES_WILDPLANTS_1, 2026-09-21. Each BiomeDef below is
       one WE author, under src/RimUtinni/UtinniPatches/Defs/BiomeDefs/, in
       THIS SAME MOD. A PatchOperationReplace here runs after that def loads
       and silently discards whatever it says - which is exactly what happened
       to RUT_Desert: nine authored plants replaced by four stale ones, and a
       live RUT_Desert map generated 0 plants of any kind against 322 on a
       vanilla Desert control tile.

       So the authored def owns its own wildPlants and this file leaves it
       alone. The rosters remain the design record; biome_flora.py's own
       check pass FAILS if an authored def and its roster disagree. The
       generator also
       cannot write MayRequire (see the note further down), and those defs
       carry 68 guarded cross-mod refs - another reason the emitter is the
       wrong owner for this field.

       RUT_AridShrubland  (10 plants, authored in its own def)
       RUT_BlueDesert  (3 plants, authored in its own def)
       RUT_Contagion  (10 plants, authored in its own def)
       RUT_CrackedLands  (6 plants, authored in its own def)
       RUT_Desert  (9 plants, authored in its own def)
       RUT_ExtremeDesert  (3 plants, authored in its own def)
       RUT_FeverWood  (7 plants, authored in its own def)
       RUT_ForsakenCrags  (8 plants, authored in its own def)
       RUT_Greentide  (11 plants, authored in its own def)
       RUT_Miasma  (4 plants, authored in its own def)
       RUT_PoisonForest  (9 plants, authored in its own def)
       RUT_RustCathedral  (0 plants, authored in its own def)
       RUT_Scarlands  (1 plants, authored in its own def)
       RUT_Slime  (5 plants, authored in its own def)
       RUT_Sump  (1 plants, authored in its own def)
       RUT_TheForge  (10 plants, authored in its own def)
       RUT_TheRot  (30 plants, authored in its own def)
       RUT_FuelSnows  (4 plants, authored in its own def — renamed from RUT_Umbra
         2026-09-21, UMBRA_IS_A_REGION_NOT_A_BIOME_1)
       RUT_Wasteland  (9 plants, authored in its own def)
       RUT_Webwork  (7 plants, authored in its own def)
       RUT_WeepingStones  (4 plants, authored in its own def)
  -->

  <!-- ============ A. dayside desert, badlands and the river jungles ============ -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="ZBiome_Grasslands"]/wildPlants</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="ZBiome_Grasslands"]/wildPlants</xpath>
      <value>
        <wildPlants>
          <RM_FE_Plant_Quickgrass>4.0</RM_FE_Plant_Quickgrass> <!-- quickgrass -->
        </wildPlants>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- ============ flora exclusions - biomes a SHARED roster does not plant ============

       These BiomeDefs appear in a roster's defNames but get NO wildPlants
       operation above, deliberately. There is nothing to patch: BiomeDef.cs
       declares `public float plantDensity;` (default 0) and `wildPlants = new
       List<BiomePlantRecord>()` (default empty), and these defs declare neither -
       so the absence of an operation IS the exclusion, and it is durable.
       biome_flora.py refuses to build if any other roster plants one of them.

       RUT_PropaneLake  (the_propane_lakes.json)
         A LIQUID-PROPANE SEA GROWS NOTHING. Ruled by BENCH, 2026-09-09 fix wave. This file's
         four flora rows are the LAND crystal flora of RUT_FuelSnows (renamed from
         AB_PropaneLakes, then from RUT_Umbra 2026-09-21 per UMBRA_IS_A_REGION_NOT_A_BIOME_1 —
         Umbra now names the region, not this biome; the fuel-snow shore, 2,531 tiles as of the
         2026-09-12 export); def-binding handed the same four to the 57 water
         tiles of RUT_PropaneLake, where the medium is liquid propane at ~-79 °C and no
         photosynthetic or crystal-accreting surface exists. The lake's life is the ruled
         propane-native exotics (the V-wake creature and kin) — creatures owed as new defs, never
         wildPlants. Same split the fauna rows already make: every fauna row here binds
         RUT_FuelSnows only.
  -->

  <!-- ============ plantDensity - the named exception list ============ -->
  <!-- RUT_Wasteland: 0.0099 -> 0.12 is carried by the AUTHORED def
       (src/RimUtinni/UtinniPatches/Defs/BiomeDefs/), not patched here.
       1,721 tiles of CONTAMINATION-class ground carrying a nine-plant toxic roster - toxigrass,
       gutter plantain, twisted dandelion, scorched stars - that exists to say THIS GROUND IS
       POISONED. At 0.0099 it says nothing. Poisoned ground reads more strongly with sick plants on
       it than with nothing. 12x up, still visibly barren.
  -->

</Patch>
